# Title: Potential Initial Access via DLL Search Order Hijacking
# ID: dbbd9f66-2ed3-4ca2-98a4-6ea985dd1a1c
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Tim Rauch (rule), Elastic (idea)
# Date: 2022-10-21
# Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.persistence, attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1566, attack.t1566.001, attack.initial-access, attack.t1574, attack.t1574.001
# Description: Detects attempts to create a DLL file to a known desktop application dependencies folder such as Slack, Teams or OneDrive and by an unusual process. This may indicate an attempt to load a malicious module via DLL search order hijacking.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((process.executable:*\\winword.exe OR process.executable:*\\excel.exe OR process.executable:*\\powerpnt.exe OR process.executable:*\\MSACCESS.EXE OR process.executable:*\\MSPUB.EXE OR process.executable:*\\fltldr.exe OR process.executable:*\\cmd.exe OR process.executable:*\\certutil.exe OR process.executable:*\\mshta.exe OR process.executable:*\\cscript.exe OR process.executable:*\\wscript.exe OR process.executable:*\\curl.exe OR process.executable:*\\powershell.exe OR process.executable:*\\pwsh.exe) AND file.path:*.dll AND (file.path:*\\Users\\* AND file.path:*\\AppData\\*) AND (file.path:*\\Microsoft\\OneDrive\\* OR file.path:*\\Microsoft OneDrive\\* OR file.path:*\\Microsoft\\Teams\\* OR file.path:*\\Local\\slack\\app-* OR file.path:*\\Local\\Programs\\Microsoft VS Code\\*)) AND NOT ((process.executable:*\\cmd.exe AND (file.path:*\\Users\\* AND file.path:*\\AppData\\* AND file.path:*\\Microsoft\\OneDrive\\* AND file.path:*\\api-ms-win-core-*))))
